<title>CHINA: Shanghai punishes firms for re-export violations.</title>
<headline>Shanghai punishes firms for re-export violations.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai customs officials have punished three foreign trading firms for failing to re-export imported goods within the allotted period, the official Xinhua news agency reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The goods involved were imported chemical fabrics, electric motors and batteries worth $250,000, it said.</p>
<p>Officials have stopped the firms' bank accounts as punishment, it said. It did not name the companies.</p>
</text>
